{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh","id":1560197,"title":"Why is the VTM version of the sunlight weakness so harsh?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-25T00:18:54-07:00","id":1560197,"title":"Why is the VTM version of the sunlight weakness so harsh?","content":"In most vampire fiction, only direct sunlight burns vampires. The Near Dark vampires sleep in indirect sunlight, and only burn when direct sunlight hits them. The Fright Night fight normally in indirect sunlight, and only burn when hit by direct sunlight. The Lost Boys sleep in a cave that has indirect sunlight, and only burn when one reaches his hand out into direct sunlight. Langella Dracula fights in a ship's hold with plenty of indirect sunlight, and only burns when dragged out into direct sunlight. Numerous Christopher Lee Draculas fight in indirect sunlight and only burn when Van Helsing manages to expose him to direct sunlight. Angel often works during the day simply by avoiding direct sunlight. <br /> <br /> They also generally heal quickly when they get out of the sunlight fast enough. There are plenty of Vampire Diaries episodes where a vampire gets badly burned by direct exposure to sunlight, they escape before dying, and the damage heals in seconds. Abigail loses a hand to direct sunlight, and then almost immediately grows it back.<br /> <br /> Why does VTM go with this incredibly harsh interpretation of the weakness where even indirect sunlight is incredibly deadly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-25-2026, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T02:19:22-07:00","id":1560199,"title":"","content":"Because it source I think<br /> See it is not the Curse of God, but the Curse of an Archangle, wroking tandem with <i>another</i> curse<br /> <br /> Raphael's - the driver of the Sun, ward of the East - curse according the Book of Nod was &quot;For as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always&quot;<br /> It is a bit of the extension of Michael's - General of Heaven, wielder of the holy Flame - curse &quot;For as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is not important what system or relegion or setting you use, be it Ra, Helios, or Raphael in WoD the Sun is perfectly capable to withold it powers, good example the Serpentis power &quot;Pact with Ra&quot; that calls upon the debt incurred when Sutek defended <i>Ra</i> against the monstrous serpent Apep.. and the Setite who uses this power until the next sunrise will be utterly unaffected by sunlight and daytime... or amplify it<br /> <br /> Raphael was the &quot;driver of the Sun&quot; or basically the embodiment of Sun in a few interpretation (matching real-world mythology, Kabbalah, where Raphael is sometimes called the Regent of the Sun)<br /> In Vampire Raphael was portrayed with strong solar associations <br /> If you go with a bit of crossovery, Demon and Werewolf, he is probably along the line of a &quot;Solar Incarna&quot; with Ra, Helios and Katanka-Sonnak<br /> But even if he &quot;just&quot; an Archangle, his Curse is a strong one and paired with Michael's<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> Anyway that curse is a strong one and with Michael's the two curses make sure your vampire ends up crispy (you can survive, of course, it is not insta-death, death is just a side effect you bruning up)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T02:20:19-07:00","id":1560200,"title":"","content":"I don't know.<br /> <br /> It's not just the sunlight, the vampire is barely able to stay awake for more than a few seconds once the sun is out. Makes the damage very situational.<br /> <br /> Aggravated makes sunlight feel like a big deal so that's good.<br /> And being unable to work during the day helps establish that kindred can only pretend to be human, they cannot truly live as a human.<br /> <br /> Without that it becomes much easier to establish a lifestyle that is inconvenient but still pretty comfortable.<br /> <br /> Thing is most games won't extrapolate only being awake at night really being a massive problem. Even in the world of darkness where everything runs 24/7.<br /> <br /> For good reason to, it's nice being able to play as a CEO and not the corpse he keeps in his basement and that feeds him blood at night. Being the mastermind behind the pawn isn't that fun at the table just means you don't get to do stuff yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T03:04:42-07:00","id":1560202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh#post1560197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most vampire fiction, only direct sunlight burns vampires. The Near Dark vampires sleep in indirect sunlight, and only burn when direct sunlight hits them. The Fright Night fight normally in indirect sunlight, and only burn when hit by direct sunlight. The Lost Boys sleep in a cave that has indirect sunlight, and only burn when one reaches his hand out into direct sunlight. Langella Dracula fights in a ship's hold with plenty of indirect sunlight, and only burns when dragged out into direct sunlight. Numerous Christopher Lee Draculas fight in indirect sunlight and only burn when Van Helsing manages to expose him to direct sunlight. Angel often works during the day simply by avoiding direct sunlight.<br /> <br /> They also generally heal quickly when they get out of the sunlight fast enough. There are plenty of Vampire Diaries episodes where a vampire gets badly burned by direct exposure to sunlight, they escape before dying, and the damage heals in seconds. Abigail loses a hand to direct sunlight, and then almost immediately grows it back.<br /> <br /> Why does VTM go with this incredibly harsh interpretation of the weakness where even indirect sunlight is incredibly deadly?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the game, <b>Vampyr</b>, sunlight doesn't actually kill vampires at all. Staying in the sun for too long will incapacitate the vampire, as their body is charred so badly it becomes immobile. But once the sun sets, they will start to regenerate again.<br /> <br /> While in the <b>Vampire's Assistant</b> novel series, sunlight kills vampires slowly. It takes roughly an hour of prolonged exposure for them to actually start burning, and somewhere around 6 hours before they're at risk of dying.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though, if you want to get scientific about it, we could say that even so much as looking at sunlight should be deadly to a vampire. Since the sun's rays would need to actually reach the vampire's eyes in order for them to even perceive daylight. But if we did that, then we'd have to make a similar case about the effects of moonlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 05-25-2026, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-30T16:27:13-07:00","id":1560277,"title":"","content":"I think it is just the game trying to achieve a &quot;balance&quot; in terms of benefits and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> While the average new PC is often frustrated by not being able to simulate all the powers of the cinematic vampire, once you have enough XP, VtM vampires often are far more powerful than any cinematic vampire. In horror movies, ordinary humans can often defeat vampires who are awake and active in that pre-sundown time. In the VtM setting, human hunters will often quickly lose unless the vampire is immobile. Or bursting in flames because of any sunlight.<br /> <br /> Any handling of that trope in any medium of fiction will be determined by one thing only: the needs of the story/plot and wishes of the author in creating their world. There's also artistic mediums that need to be considered. Movies and television shows need a certain amount of light so scenes can be captured on film and the audience can see them. So having actors move around while there is still some daylight left is absolutely necessary when in places where there would not be ambient artificial light.<br /> <br /> Personally when I used Mortis as its own (heavily rewritten) Discipline instead of converting it into Necromancy, I used that power as a way for vampires to be active in the daytime albeit at the cost of losing most of their supernatural powers. At the lowest level it would make their sleeping body be a normal corpse that would not explode in flame, and at higher levels would allow the vampire to be active around sundown and sunrise while daylight was still present albeit at the loss of most powers, and finally to the level of Dracula where the vampire could be completely active and unharmed in daytime although without any use of powers. It was a way to include these kinds of cinematic and literary scenes into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T07:05:19-07:00","id":1560370,"title":"","content":"I think the idea was to make the weakness of a vampire really impactful and hard to ignore. But imo they really overdid it in cases.<br /> <br /> VTM Vampires RAW would probably not work all the well in movies and TV.<br /> <br /> I think that a lot of movies and especially TV series tone down the weakness to sunlight is not that convenient to shoot entire TV series in the Dark, and will like ramp up the cost.<br /> <br /> The blood consumption of other fictional vampires tends also to much lower than the one of VTM vampires. I a more action packed movie or series the protagonist would need to consume massive amounts of blood after each action scene to refill the blood pool if they follow VTM rules.<br /> <br /> Btw. iirc even the 90s VTM TV series toned the weakness of vampires down quite lot compared to the game, I would not be surprised if VTM novels would do the same (but I haven't read any).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T04:45:58-07:00","id":1560451,"title":"","content":"The simple answer is that the writers didn't think that far ahead on how it would actually function as a world building fact. They also made a lot of the classic weaknesses into optional flaws (silver and garlic) or removed them entirely (needs an invitation and can't cross running water). In some cases that was good (looking at you running water weakness) and in others it can be argued to be bad (silver and garlic). As Aahz pointed out, the blood pool is also worth mentioning as an example of things that don't really work out that well when you have to think it through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T05:47:25-07:00","id":1560453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560451#post1560451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simple answer is that the writers didn't think that far ahead on how it would actually function as a world building fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's plausible to claim the writers haven't thought about it. As a harsh weakness it's made its way through five editions as well as jumping to <i>Requiem</i>. There have been many opportunities to change it, or at least tone it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T08:34:57-07:00","id":1560457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560277#post1560277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the average new PC is often frustrated by not being able to simulate all the powers of the cinematic vampire, once you have enough XP, VtM vampires often are far more powerful than any cinematic vampire. In horror movies, ordinary humans can often defeat vampires who are awake and active in that pre-sundown time. In the VtM setting, human hunters will often quickly lose unless the vampire is immobile. Or bursting in flames because of any sunlight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeh. The thing is, movie/tv vampires often have powers that would require an huge number of Discipline dots, and can use them far more routinely than Hunger or Blood Points allows in-game. It's not that they are less powerful, so much as the human heroes have plot-armor. The vampires will do things like casually flip over cars, bend steel bars, shatter thick wooden beams, and one-shot nameless extras. Somehow when it comes to the heroes, though, all they can do is throw them around until the hero stakes them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T16:51:47-07:00","id":1560463,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T17:02:57-07:00","id":1560465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560451#post1560451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simple answer is that the writers didn't think that far ahead on how it would actually function as a world building fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the weakness to sunlight it not functional to world building?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T17:06:00-07:00","id":1560467,"title":"","content":"Can't Fortitude be used to soak Aggravated damage?<br /> <br /> So that with a high enough level of mastery, you can just flat out tank sunlight?<br /> <br /> I don't think you can do that in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T17:11:24-07:00","id":1560468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560370#post1560370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The blood consumption of other fictional vampires tends also to much lower than the one of VTM vampires. I a more action packed movie or series the protagonist would need to consume massive amounts of blood after each action scene to refill the blood pool if they follow VTM rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the blood consumption of most fictional vampires tends towards &quot;feeds on people until they're dead all the time&quot;, whereas the typical vampire in Masquerade has enough blood points to account for about one and a half people and there's a categorical setting element of cultivating environments in which they can feed on a larger number of people more sustainably.<br /> <br /> Like, three people fed on until they'll be woozy for the next couple of weeks would refill a blood pool (danger of Frenzy notwithstanding).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T20:09:30-07:00","id":1560470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560468#post1560468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though the blood consumption of most fictional vampires tends towards &quot;feeds on people until they're dead all the time&quot;, whereas the typical vampire in Masquerade has enough blood points to account for about one and a half people and there's a categorical setting element of cultivating environments in which they can feed on a larger number of people more sustainably.<br /> <br /> Like, three people fed on until they'll be woozy for the next couple of weeks would refill a blood pool (danger of Frenzy notwithstanding).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm positive that with the exception of saliva and eye fluids, all other liquid contained within the vampire's body is converted into vitae. Meaning that their bodies contain A LOT more blood than what any normal human should be capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T22:45:47-07:00","id":1560472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560468#post1560468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the blood consumption of most fictional vampires tends towards &quot;feeds on people until they're dead all the time&quot;, whereas the typical vampire in Masquerade has enough blood points to account for about one and a half people and there's a categorical setting element of cultivating environments in which they can feed on a larger number of people more sustainably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends of of really on the franchise. And depends of course also a lot on if the Vampires are the protgonists or the bad guys.<br /> <br /> If I look at something like Underworld, Selene would likely need to start feeding mid fight or assuming that she is likely pretty low gen drink multiple humans dry after each fight, if she was folowing VTM Rules.<br /> <br /> And while healing regular damage isn't that costly for VTM Vampires healing agg damage also requires a lot of blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560468#post1560468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, three people fed on until they'll be woozy for the next couple of weeks would refill a blood pool (danger of Frenzy notwithstanding).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is just to find those 3 people fast enough. Doing multiple fights or action scenes right after one another without feeding in between is hard in VTM. You pump a few attributes, use a bit celerity or some other discipline powers and heal some damage and your blood pools is pretty much gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 06-09-2026, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T23:25:29-07:00","id":1560473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560453#post1560453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's plausible to claim the writers haven't thought about it. As a harsh weakness it's made its way through five editions as well as jumping to <i>Requiem</i>. There have been many opportunities to change it, or at least tone it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't speaking of later writers. Only the very first ones. Later ones could've had plenty of reasons to keep that they simply haven't told us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560465#post1560465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the weakness to sunlight it not functional to world building?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that it isn't functional. Just that my impression is that they didn't think that far ahead when it comes to how it impacts it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T23:38:58-07:00","id":1560475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560473#post1560473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't speaking of later writers. Only the very first ones. Later ones could've had plenty of reasons to keep that they simply haven't told us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so what are you basing this on?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T00:15:18-07:00","id":1560477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560475#post1560475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so what are you basing this on?</div> </div> </div> </div> My own impressions based on how it would impact vampires ability to hide amongst mortals. Including making claims like them being gods (sun god in one instance IIRC) when they can't even enter sunlight or stay up during the day without significant effort. All of which grows increasingly difficult after the industrial age and everything becomes much more documented. Nearly everything operates during day outside of specific professions, and even those will sooner or later deal with having to be active during daylight for things like a meeting. A lot of them being important to maintaining a mortal identity, such as various government services that they need to interact with. With some countries being harder or easier depending on their specific circumstances. There's also the fact that any amount of direct sunlight is enough to instantly reveal them, which remains true even if they're one of the few with high enough fortitude to soak the damage in full.<br /> <br /> It takes a lot of work do deal with just how crippling a sunlight weakness as harsh as VtM's is, especially in the modern world. A world infamous for not being very accommodating to people with needs outside of the norm. This gets even worse the more scrutinized your vocation is, such as that of a CEO where you essentially need to be on call 24/7 in the modern world. With everyone paying attention to the things you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T05:52:03-07:00","id":1560483,"title":"","content":"Well the only sensible explanation for this weakness is that one of the authors got a supremely bad sunburn at some point and decided to dedicate a whole game line to the noble endeavour of teaching future generations to regard Sol as a terror and a mortal enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T18:40:54-07:00","id":1560500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560477#post1560477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My own impressions based on how it would impact vampires ability to hide amongst mortals. Including making claims like them being gods (sun god in one instance IIRC) when they can't even enter sunlight or stay up during the day without significant effort. All of which grows increasingly difficult after the industrial age and everything becomes much more documented. Nearly everything operates during day outside of specific professions, and even those will sooner or later deal with having to be active during daylight for things like a meeting. A lot of them being important to maintaining a mortal identity, such as various government services that they need to interact with. With some countries being harder or easier depending on their specific circumstances. There's also the fact that any amount of direct sunlight is enough to instantly reveal them, which remains true even if they're one of the few with high enough fortitude to soak the damage in full.<br /> <br /> It takes a lot of work do deal with just how crippling a sunlight weakness as harsh as VtM's is, especially in the modern world. A world infamous for not being very accommodating to people with needs outside of the norm. This gets even worse the more scrutinized your vocation is, such as that of a CEO where you essentially need to be on call 24/7 in the modern world. With everyone paying attention to the things you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered that the various flavours of mind control that vampires have access to might have been considered relative to the level of influence they can exert while having such limited activity times?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T18:47:06-07:00","id":1560501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560470#post1560470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm positive that with the exception of saliva and eye fluids, all other liquid contained within the vampire's body is converted into vitae. Meaning that their bodies contain A LOT more blood than what any normal human should be capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That argument seems irrelevant to the fact that Vitae is a resource in the game mechanics, with a quantifiable basis for how it relates to impacting people's health while replenishing it.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm pretty sure that every single Vampire game maintains that &quot;having a hundred points of Vitae doesn't mean that the really powerful vampires are bursting at the seams with the equivalent of the blood of thirteen people, it means that the consumed blood becomes mystically concentrated and potent&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560472#post1560472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I look at something like Underworld, Selene would likely need to start feeding mid fight or assuming that she is likely pretty low gen drink multiple humans dry after each fight, if she was folowing VTM Rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the VTM rules really adapted for the same extent of high flying kung fu action in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is just to find those 3 people fast enough. Doing multiple fights or action scenes right after one another without feeding in between is hard in VTM. You pump a few attributes, use a bit celerity or some other discipline powers and heal some damage and your blood pools is pretty much gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this does make a comment on how the rules aren't well calibrated to a scenario that is atypical of the setting and the general intended play experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T20:13:18-07:00","id":1560503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560501#post1560501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That argument seems irrelevant to the fact that Vitae is a resource in the game mechanics, with a quantifiable basis for how it relates to impacting people's health while replenishing it.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm pretty sure that every single Vampire game maintains that &quot;having a hundred points of Vitae doesn't mean that the really powerful vampires are bursting at the seams with the equivalent of the blood of thirteen people, it means that the consumed blood becomes mystically concentrated and potent&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I can understand the wisdom of that, don't the books explain that a fully gorged vampire will have a bloated and flushed appearance, while a starving vampire will become more withered and dried out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T23:28:38-07:00","id":1560506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560500#post1560500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you considered that the various flavours of mind control that vampires have access to might have been considered relative to the level of influence they can exert while having such limited activity times?</div> </div> </div> </div>Occam's razor. In short it won't work for the simple reason that there's too many humans to deal with. We're speaking of everything from corporate executives to independent journalists.<br /> <br /> If you want a taste of how difficult this would actually be, then run a campaign where every player is a vampire CEO with the ST actively working on bringing down the Masquerade to kickstart the Second Inquisition without resorting to any sort of cheating. And this would still fall short of how many variables they'd have to contend with in a realistic scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T02:17:25-07:00","id":1560509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560501#post1560501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the VTM rules really adapted for the same extent of high flying kung fu action in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity (and a lot of other combat powers) exist.<br /> You can do pretty crazy kung fu action stuff, just not very sustainably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560501#post1560501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess this does make a comment on how the rules aren't well calibrated to a scenario that is atypical of the setting and the general intended play experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the question was VTM Vampires vs Fictonal Vampires, and Fictional Vampires seem not to run out of gas that quickly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T02:29:00-07:00","id":1560510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560506#post1560506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Occam's razor. In short it won't work for the simple reason that there's too many humans to deal with. We're speaking of everything from corporate executives to independent journalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orrrrr, instead of interpreting it in terms of &quot;controlling every single person you might need to interact with&quot;, it could be seen in terms of controlling a very small number of people who can function as proxies during the day.<br /> <br /> What are ghouls for?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T03:03:47-07:00","id":1560511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560510#post1560510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Orrrrr, instead of interpreting it in terms of &quot;controlling every single person you might need to interact with&quot;, it could be seen in terms of controlling a very small number of people who can function as proxies during the day.<br /> <br /> What are ghouls for?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The same problems remain for the vampire CEO. You're still only one solar ray away from discovery and people will eventually question why you aren't awake during the day if you hold any sort of office where you're expected to interact with people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T05:08:18-07:00","id":1560515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560509#post1560509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity (and a lot of other combat powers) exist.<br /> You can do pretty crazy kung fu action stuff, just not very sustainably.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the question was VTM Vampires vs Fictonal Vampires, and Fictional Vampires seem not to run out of gas that quickly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The power of super speed / time control is so overpowered, that the only reason any conflict should be a challenge for you, is if you are a total imbecile with how you utilize it.<br /> <br /> You can cross a room and chop a guy's head off before he even has time to finish half a blink. If he manages to defeat you, it's because you were dicking around too much.<br /> <br /> Super Strength or Durability isn't going to protect them either, when they get clocked with a punch exceeding Mach 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T08:16:09-07:00","id":1560521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560510#post1560510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Orrrrr, instead of interpreting it in terms of &quot;controlling every single person you might need to interact with&quot;, it could be seen in terms of controlling a very small number of people who can function as proxies during the day.<br /> <br /> What are ghouls for?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cWhatever we tell them to do and also whatever we need them to do, whether we tell them or not.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWhat happens if they don\u2019t know what you need them to do when you don\u2019t tell them?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> \u201cI give them a stern talking-to and then start looking for new ghouls.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T11:58:58-07:00","id":1560553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560511#post1560511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same problems remain for the vampire CEO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there an abundance of vampire CEOs in this setting?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T15:33:31-07:00","id":1560589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560553#post1560553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there an abundance of vampire CEOs in this setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't change the argument whether there is or not.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a friend pointed out to me, its claimed to be more than enough of them, including government employee ones, to enforce the global conspiracy that is the masquerade. Something that would in fact just make it far more likely to be discovered than if they'd stayed in the darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13674,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","user":"Amalasuintha","date":". 06-12-2026, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T07:13:30-07:00","id":1560597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560511#post1560511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same problems remain for the vampire CEO. You're still only one solar ray away from discovery and people will eventually question why you aren't awake during the day if you hold any sort of office where you're expected to interact with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really?<br /> <br /> We do have a day / night shift patrol in real life. A lot of people sleep during the day and only go to work at night.<br /> <br /> Heck, we even have schools that are only active at night!<br /> <br /> And if you're rich / high ranking enough, it would be child's play to wave off any pesky day time interruptions, by having your ghouled 'secretary' handle any social interactions in your stead.<br /> <br /> You're a busy vampire; you've got important shit to do. If somebody wants to bother you with a meeting, you tell them to book an appointment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T11:31:48-07:00","id":1560599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560597#post1560597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really?<br /> <br /> We do have a day / night shift patrol in real life. A lot of people sleep during the day and only go to work at night.<br /> <br /> Heck, we even have schools that are only active at night!<br /> <br /> And if you're rich / high ranking enough, it would be child's play to wave off any pesky day time interruptions, by having your ghouled 'secretary' handle any social interactions in your stead.<br /> <br /> You're a busy vampire; you've got important shit to do. If somebody wants to bother you with a meeting, you tell them to book an appointment.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't change the overall math any still as I already took it into account, especially since these are not shift jobs. The vast majority of important people are humans. The vampire won't be able to handle it this way with most of those in their class. Let alone anyone in positions higher like than that, like ministers, heads of governments and heads of states. Every vampire that wants to do something like this, is on a countdown time to discovery. Its not a question of if, its a question of when. A sunlight weakness as harsh as VTM's reduces said countdown significantly.<br /> <br /> Never mind all the issues that'd crop up if they got involved in a court case. There's a reason this sort of thing was one of the Gehenna scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T14:52:01-07:00","id":1560602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560599#post1560599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This doesn't change the overall math any still as I already took it into account, especially since these are not shift jobs. The vast majority of important people are humans. The vampire won't be able to handle it this way with most of those in their class. Let alone anyone in positions higher like than that, like ministers, heads of governments and heads of states. Every vampire that wants to do something like this, is on a countdown time to discovery. Its not a question of if, its a question of when. A sunlight weakness as harsh as VTM's reduces said countdown significantly.<br /> <br /> Never mind all the issues that'd crop up if they got involved in a court case. There's a reason this sort of thing was one of the Gehenna scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I guess the entirety of clans Ventrue, Toreador, Lasombra and Giovanni can just eat crow then?<br /> <br /> Because I'm pretty sure they've built their entire clan identities around infiltrating the upper echelons of society, influencing public perception, and running secret, criminal empires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T15:33:36-07:00","id":1560603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560602#post1560602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I guess the entirety of clans Ventrue, Toreador, Lasombra and Giovanni can just eat crow then?<br /> <br /> Because I'm pretty sure they've built their entire clan identities around infiltrating the upper echelons of society, influencing public perception, and running secret, criminal empires.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all doomed to fail and that was part of the plot all along. The grander the conspiracy, the quicker it dies. A harsh sunlight weakness like the one in VTM means it'll happen faster than a setting without one. That's part of the point of the whole doomsday is coming metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T15:54:36-07:00","id":1560604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560603#post1560603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're all doomed to fail and that was part of the plot all along. The grander the conspiracy, the quicker it dies. A harsh sunlight weakness like the one in VTM means it'll happen faster than a setting without one. That's part of the point of the whole doomsday is coming metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps if you go with the most mild mannered, milk toast, down to earth version of doomsday scenario.<br /> <br /> But such clans have been able to maintain their positions within human society for decades, if not centuries without being discovered.<br /> <br /> The only reason it came to an end, is because older, hungrier monsters from the dawn of time woke up and decided to go on a rampage.<br /> <br /> That's not really the fault of the vampires being unable to blend in with society. It's a case of the (metaphorical) Story Teller deciding to flip the table and declare the campaign is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T00:25:22-07:00","id":1560612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560604#post1560604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps if you go with the most mild mannered, milk toast, down to earth version of doomsday scenario.<br /> <br /> But such clans have been able to maintain their positions within human society for decades, if not centuries without being discovered.<br /> <br /> The only reason it came to an end, is because older, hungrier monsters from the dawn of time woke up and decided to go on a rampage.<br /> <br /> That's not really the fault of the vampires being unable to blend in with society. It's a case of the (metaphorical) Story Teller deciding to flip the table and declare the campaign is over.</div> </div> </div> </div>A conspiracy this large never survives due to there being too many failure points and it only becomes harder as technology advances. That's before pointing out we live in a neurotypical world where any accommodation had to be fought for with sweat and blood. Its been part of the setting from the start vamps are just one screw up away from the whole house of cards collapsing according to White Wolf themselves. Its part of their intent to create the whole &quot;Gehenna is coming&quot; atmosphere of the entire setting and its canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T05:24:04-07:00","id":1560615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560612#post1560612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A conspiracy this large never survives due to there being too many failure points and it only becomes harder as technology advances. That's before pointing out we live in a neurotypical world where any accommodation had to be fought for with sweat and blood. Its been part of the setting from the start vamps are just one screw up away from the whole house of cards collapsing according to White Wolf themselves. Its part of their intent to create the whole &quot;Gehenna is coming&quot; atmosphere of the entire setting and its canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, most of the Gehenna scenarios came about because the literal <b>end of the world</b> happened. By that same logic, no system of governance was ultimately sustainable.<br /> <br /> Does it really matter if they would have been found out <b>eventually</b>, if they managed to stay hidden until the final hour?<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, one of the Gehenna scenarios demonstrates that the overarching fear of humanity rising up against them was ultimately just mass hysteria. Humans declaring full blown war upon the supernatural is exactly what happens, only for it to result in mutual destruction. The mortals were not prepared for a simultaneous conflict against Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Fae, Wraiths, Demons, Mummies, and whatever other splats were involved at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T05:37:15-07:00","id":1560616,"title":"","content":"It's more a matter of how you implement the setting than what the setting is.<br /> <br /> It's almost like toggles in a computer game. Like when you start some 4x grand strategy extravaganza and you get to check a bunch of switches for how grevious the winter is or how difficult it is to replenish troops or how unreasonable diplomacy is.<br /> <br /> You have some premise - the Ventrue exerts influence over mortal institutions, but how they do that is somewhat ambiguous and sometimes contradictory. When you start a new run - chronicle - what toggles do you switch on? <br /> <br /> How difficult the masquerade is to maintain is another toggle. <br /> <br /> I wonder how you could make a difficult to maintain masquerade and still have a fun game. Paranoia and tension could be great but it feels difficult to implement in gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T11:16:32-07:00","id":1560621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560616#post1560616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder how you could make a difficult to maintain masquerade and still have a fun game. Paranoia and tension could be great but it feels difficult to implement in gameplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind you that one of the fanon nicknames for World of Darkness was <i>&quot;Katanas and Trenchcoats,&quot;</i> because a lot of games ended up turning into Blade / The Matrix style fight sequences.<br /> <br /> The whole political espionage gameplay didn't seem to catch on that well. I guess when your most commonly available disciplines are heavily combat focused, constantly playing 4D chess against the NPC's gets frustrating.<br /> <br /> Plus, it probably doesn't help that the sects are thinly veiled coding for real life politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T11:59:27-07:00","id":1560623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560621#post1560621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mind you that one of the fanon nicknames for World of Darkness was <i>&quot;Katanas and Trenchcoats,&quot;</i> because a lot of games ended up turning into Blade / The Matrix style fight sequences.<br /> <br /> The whole political espionage gameplay didn't seem to catch on that well. I guess when your most commonly available disciplines are heavily combat focused, constantly playing 4D chess against the NPC's gets frustrating.<br /> <br /> Plus, it probably doesn't help that the sects are thinly veiled coding for real life politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's nice that the game is both versatile and takes inspiration from real world history, politics, and philosophy (and fiction). Gives you a lot of meat so to speak when you run the game. <br /> <br /> It's good for action to as long as you sidestep the combat system to the right degree. But the easiest to run is always investigation and social interaction.<br /> <br /> Political espionage is not as straightforward...<br /> but you know Ars Magica had this structure of large segments of time passing where you did some adventuring and then seasons changed and stuff.<br /> <br /> And what can be gleaned of that Tremere campaign that preceded VtM they did seem to host a lot of political espionage. ..and action come to think of it.<br /> <br /> So maybe one solution is to adopt an Ars Magica style structure to the game, give players lots of rope to do what they will, have months pass between adventures, have a shift of perspectives between elders and neonates and ghouls...<br /> <br /> And then you could ratchet up the implications of sunlight, explore how the players play into institutions, make the masquerade dangerous to breach (hunters or internal punishment, less breaking the setting more breaking the characters if they become careless).<br /> <br /> Bit of work to implement though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T14:48:27-07:00","id":1560624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560623#post1560623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's nice that the game is both versatile and takes inspiration from real world history, politics, and philosophy (and fiction). Gives you a lot of meat so to speak when you run the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, until you find yourself on the political side that the game keeps screaming <i>&quot;these are the bad guys, and you should hate them!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560623#post1560623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So maybe one solution is to adopt an Ars Magica style structure to the game, give players lots of rope to do what they will, have months pass between adventures, have a shift of perspectives between elders and neonates and ghouls...<br /> <br /> And then you could ratchet up the implications of sunlight, explore how the players play into institutions, make the masquerade dangerous to breach (hunters or internal punishment, less breaking the setting more breaking the characters if they become careless).<br /> <br /> Bit of work to implement though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I should probably check out Ars Magica sometime. I've heard the name tossed around a lot, but never really bothered to learn about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T15:32:17-07:00","id":1560626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560624#post1560624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should probably check out Ars Magica sometime. I've heard the name tossed around a lot, but never really bothered to learn about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If VtM hadn't been so successful maybe they'd have published a ton more Ars Magica stuff and it'd have been in the same place as Call of Cthulhu or Traveller or any other truly long running game that isn't DND.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T16:04:15-07:00","id":1560627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560615#post1560615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, most of the Gehenna scenarios came about because the literal <b>end of the world</b> happened. By that same logic, no system of governance was ultimately sustainable.<br /> <br /> Does it really matter if they would have been found out <b>eventually</b>, if they managed to stay hidden until the final hour?<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, one of the Gehenna scenarios demonstrates that the overarching fear of humanity rising up against them was ultimately just mass hysteria. Humans declaring full blown war upon the supernatural is exactly what happens, only for it to result in mutual destruction. The mortals were not prepared for a simultaneous conflict against Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Fae, Wraiths, Demons, Mummies, and whatever other splats were involved at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've no idea what you're even arguing at this point. I wasn't speaking of the supernatural gehenna scenarios. Just the one that sends vampires running for the hills due to the inevitable discovery happening and the cover up failing. Which was part of my wider point that the harsh sunlight weakness plays into how quickly that house of cards would fall apart due to how easily a fuck up can happen in a world that's utterly horrid at accommodating anyone with needs beyond the standard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560616#post1560616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more a matter of how you implement the setting than what the setting is.<br /> <br /> It's almost like toggles in a computer game. Like when you start some 4x grand strategy extravaganza and you get to check a bunch of switches for how grevious the winter is or how difficult it is to replenish troops or how unreasonable diplomacy is.<br /> <br /> You have some premise - the Ventrue exerts influence over mortal institutions, but how they do that is somewhat ambiguous and sometimes contradictory. When you start a new run - chronicle - what toggles do you switch on?<br /> <br /> How difficult the masquerade is to maintain is another toggle.<br /> <br /> I wonder how you could make a difficult to maintain masquerade and still have a fun game. Paranoia and tension could be great but it feels difficult to implement in gameplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>You definitely can't treat it with real world logic. The masquerade simply wouldn't last long in such a scenario, but that's just the problem with grand conspiracy narratives in general in fiction. They work because its just that, fiction. Suspend disbelief and enjoy it for what it is, which is what I do with such things. Doesn't mean I won't poke fun at it when chatting with people I know since that too is part of the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T19:57:15-07:00","id":1560628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560627#post1560627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've no idea what you're even arguing at this point. I wasn't speaking of the supernatural gehenna scenarios. Just the one that sends vampires running for the hills due to the inevitable discovery happening and the cover up failing. Which was part of my wider point that the harsh sunlight weakness plays into how quickly that house of cards would fall apart due to how easily a fuck up can happen in a world that's utterly horrid at accommodating anyone with needs beyond the standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm arguing is that you're claiming that the way vampires conduct themselves is not sustainable in the long term, and that Gehenna was meant to emphasize that.<br /> <br /> My counter point, to this, is that the system lasted for centuries, and only came to an end because the writers metaphorically blew up the planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mortals:</b> <i>&quot;Hah, you monsters thought you could hide forever?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Splats:</b> <i>&quot;In case you haven't noticed, the planet is on fire; we don't need to anymore!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560627#post1560627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You definitely can't treat it with real world logic. The masquerade simply wouldn't last long in such a scenario, but that's just the problem with grand conspiracy narratives in general in fiction. They work because its just that, fiction. Suspend disbelief and enjoy it for what it is, which is what I do with such things. Doesn't mean I won't poke fun at it when chatting with people I know since that too is part of the experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit confused as to what exactly you think vampires (or other splats) are doing in these scenarios. Because it seems to me like you're expecting a vampire to go full blown Dracula, shielding themselves behind a cape and hissing between sentences. And no vampire is going to be working at the office during daylight hours. They're going to clock out and let the next shift take over, while they get some much needed rest back at the haven.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires spent centuries, at least 800 years worth, building an infrastructure that was designed for the singular purpose of keeping the world ignorant of their existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even Sabbat run domains like Detroit, New York, and Mexico City, where crime was rampant, still had a Masquerade in place, because the living conditions were so terrible, that nobody noticed the literal vampires running around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T20:25:45-07:00","id":1560629,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm sure it's a design choice. There are, however, some ways to deal with the sun (like some amalgams, advanced powers and rituals etc) and really powerful vampires can basically ignore it. <br /> It's has always been like this, weak vampires are meant to be really weak and then there are vampires who are gods, pretty similar to Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles where the most powerful vampires have ways to deal with it or are basically completely immune and are essentially gods. IIRC there's a book where I read that the storyteller could decide to change it in anyway he feels, just like the Golden Rule let you ignore basically any rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T21:27:21-07:00","id":1560631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560629#post1560629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm sure it's a design choice. There are, however, some ways to deal with the sun (like some amalgams, advanced powers and rituals etc) and really powerful vampires can basically ignore it.<br /> It's has always been like this, weak vampires are meant to be really weak and then there are vampires who are gods, pretty similar to Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles where the most powerful vampires have ways to deal with it or are basically completely immune and are essentially gods. IIRC there's a book where I read that the storyteller could decide to change it in anyway he feels, just like the Golden Rule let you ignore basically any rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While this technically falls within the Requiem setting, there was a live play campaign where the sunlight weakness was done away with completely, along with the Masquerade also being completely torn down.<br /> <br /> In exchange for these radical changes, the governments of the world created a new division of law enforcement that were specifically tasked with taking down supernatural criminals.<br /> <br /> It also lead to the formation of some human centric hate groups, that took on the role of Hunters dispensing vigilante justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 06-15-2026, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T11:18:01-07:00","id":1560638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560628#post1560628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm arguing is that you're claiming that the way vampires conduct themselves is not sustainable in the long term, and that Gehenna was meant to emphasize that.<br /> <br /> My counter point, to this, is that the system lasted for centuries, and only came to an end because the writers metaphorically blew up the planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mortals:</b> <i>&quot;Hah, you monsters thought you could hide forever?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Splats:</b> <i>&quot;In case you haven't noticed, the planet is on fire; we don't need to anymore!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm a bit confused as to what exactly you think vampires (or other splats) are doing in these scenarios. Because it seems to me like you're expecting a vampire to go full blown Dracula, shielding themselves behind a cape and hissing between sentences. And no vampire is going to be working at the office during daylight hours. They're going to clock out and let the next shift take over, while they get some much needed rest back at the haven.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires spent centuries, at least 800 years worth, building an infrastructure that was designed for the singular purpose of keeping the world ignorant of their existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even Sabbat run domains like Detroit, New York, and Mexico City, where crime was rampant, still had a Masquerade in place, because the living conditions were so terrible, that nobody noticed the literal vampires running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the masquerade is not sustainable and never has been. That's the problem with any conspiracy that involves a lot of people. Especially when those involved has so many special needs. You're also the only one who's been bringing up the non-New Inquisition Gehenna scenarios and whom keeps doing it.<br /> <br /> If strawmen is what you need to invent to argue against then this conversation has run its course. I hope you have a pleasant year and many good campaigns. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T11:50:06-07:00","id":1560640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560638#post1560638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also the only one who's been bringing up the non-New Inquisition Gehenna scenarios and whom keeps doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because the New Inquisition scenario is bull shit, and I refuse to accept it.<br /> <br /> And nobody can fault me for that, because the old scenarios were multiple choice options. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T04:07:13-07:00","id":1560703,"title":"","content":"I think both are very poor lines of argument, to try to say the Masquerade makes sense because it worked for centuries in the world of make believe, and to close focus on sunlight being a big reason it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> On why so harsh? A number of reasons, but none is terribly important. It's setting flavor, few to no balancing benefits come from this, changing it in anyway or removing entirely will ruffle a lot of feathers but not make your game less fun, balanced, or true to source.<br /> <br /> Some actual reasons:<br /> 1. D&amp;D was still the default for this kind of reference at the time, especially for creatures that have no actual legend outside pop culture. In it vampires die under sunlight in a few turns.<br /> 2. Focus on the night life aesthetics. They want a game of nocturnal action, period, even if with protagonists that don't see in the dark and face abject fear at the sight of any source of light prior to power stations.<br /> 3. Making mortals dangerous. As much as the PCs are powerful, and aside the many players who would be happier with a D&amp;D adaptation but are too cool for that, the premise of high lethality is important to the game design, and the sun is the best reason to fear mortals.<br /> 4. Pedantic assumptions. A lot of VtM players are the kind that think weaknesses and harsh constraints aren't just fun to play, but actually mark them as superior artists, and that include our old pal Rein-Hagen, so that's that.<br /> 5. Tradition. Time tends to consolidate decisions that aren't too directly damaging. At this point the harshness is a lot of the identity of the game. Not something it really needs, not something everyone cares (or should), but it is something a lot of people wouldn't feel like they're playing VtM if it changed.<br /> <br /> All said and done, I think it's a problem, but for another reason: it severely limits options for actual play. Plenty of interesting story options could use a PC that can wander at day, even if in a limited capacity. Very few really benefit from a PC that badly needs electric light to be a functional person because any other light, even if dim, is a potential death sentence.<br /> <br /> Best thing they did in Requiem 2nd Ed was to make daylight far easier to endure, and no one suddenly stopped making vampire society nocturnal because of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Special powers are no solution. It doesn't matter if a dozen Disciplines change the basic constraints, the question isn't &quot;how character X can take a tan in the beach every other Saturday or navigate total darkness&quot;. It's why the basic constraints are what they are and how it affects the setting.<br /> <br /> Listing optional traits that let you not engage with the question is a wonderful way of missing the point.<br /> <br /> Watsonian explanations on why the Curse is so terrible equally miss the fact this is about design decisions by several kilometers.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't exist, not even in legends, no one was cursed by YHWH and his lovecraftian envoys who are sometimes mistaken for guys with wings, even if you believe they are real. This is a convention from within the game, not its cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 06-18-2026, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T04:20:30-07:00","id":1560704,"title":"","content":"Most of my vampire lore comes from ttrpgs, so it never occurred to me that the sunlight weakness in Vampire the Masquerade was particularly harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T04:33:18-07:00","id":1560707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560704#post1560704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my vampire lore comes from ttrpgs, so it never occurred to me that the sunlight weakness in Vampire the Masquerade was particularly harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prior to the movie Nosferatu (the original by Murnau) it wasn't even a thing. In the book Dracula has a few inconveniences during the day, none related to sunlight itself. Other early vampires, not even that (Dracula was 4th or 5th to appear, although the main trope-definer).<br /> <br /> Sure most media adopted Murnau's idea for several reasons, but usually the problem is only direct sunlight, because it's dramatic. A vampire that's terribly lethargic at day or cooks with just sufficient sunlight to read a sign is not really great for interesting scenes be as enemy or protagonist.<br /> <br /> Twilight is far less disruptive than goth purists think, and that again ruffles a lot of feathers. Though tbh, most purists of Goth aren't fans of Goth, they just want reasons to demean girly literature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T14:33:54-07:00","id":1560721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560707#post1560707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prior to the movie Nosferatu (the original by Murnau) it wasn't even a thing. In the book Dracula has a few inconveniences during the day, none related to sunlight itself. Other early vampires, not even that (Dracula was 4th or 5th to appear, although the main trope-definer).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually kind of funny to think about how the length of time between the publication of Dracula and release of Nosferatu is short enough that Bram Stoker's widow was still alive (hence why she was able to get a court order for all copies of the film to be destroyed).<br /> <br /> Compared to the fact that the time between the release of the original Nosferatu movie and the most recent remake of it is longer than an entire century.<br /> <br /> Which is to say &quot;prior to the movie Nosferatu&quot; doesn't count for much when subsequent to the movie Nosferatu is longer than an entire century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T15:39:35-07:00","id":1560725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560703#post1560703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think both are very poor lines of argument, to try to say the Masquerade makes sense because it worked for centuries in the world of make believe, and to close focus on sunlight being a big reason it wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify something: I wasn't claiming that its the biggest. Just that it would be one of the parts where things could easily go wrong very quickly due to how harsh it is. For reasons why the masquerade will fail eventually, I'd first point towards the reasons conspiracies fall apart in real life. The main one being that the bigger they get, the bigger the chance of things going completely sideways. Especially when you start adding modern technology into the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T17:39:56-07:00","id":1560731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560721#post1560721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is to say &quot;prior to the movie Nosferatu&quot; doesn't count for much when subsequent to the movie Nosferatu is longer than an entire century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, but it stands that while the notion is classic, it isn't universal, far from it, much less in the specific VtM form.<br /> <br /> The quintessential original quartet, so to speak: Lord Ruthven, Varney, Carmilla and Dracula, all prefer the night for one reason or another but are not bothered by daylight. The three proto-vampires Oneiza, Geraldine and Augustus Darvel don't show any hint in this direction, either.<br /> <br /> It's true that Nosferatu was released only 25 years after Dracula, but it was 103 after The Vampyre and 122 after Christabel.<br /> <br /> Even in later works the problem persists that it rarely if ever hit any of the two other notes we see in VtM, the lethargy and the indirect light, because more even than the idea of the weakness, what gets strong traction is the scene itself of the sudden exposure to direct sunlight getting the monster by surprise.<br /> <br /> And almost immediately after Nosferatu establishes the sunlight weakness, there start to appear the trope of the vampire who can total or partially overcome it as a sign of strength, a trope VtM is not immune to but has considerable more resistance. When Rice's Queen of the Damned does it, she's already nothing new in this regard.<br /> <br /> While I find Twilight terribly written and the sparkling skin comically silly, it is truer to the actual tradition by making the vampires avoid the day for weird convenience than VtM is when making the day so thoroughly inimical to the undead existence.<br /> <br /> None of this means the idea isn't cool, and as I said it is part of the game's identity nowadays. But it is &quot;VtM&quot;, not &quot;vampires&quot;, and the reason is not any tradition, it's just Rein-Hagen wanted, for good or I'll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560725#post1560725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify something: I wasn't claiming that its the biggest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but I don't think it big at all, not even 10th place.<br /> <br /> For the extent of their weakness to be even noticed you already have to go through a dozen or more other things that would have revealed them.<br /> <br /> People rarely or never seen during the day aren't that common. If you look the habits of rich and/or important people IRL through history you'll see several weirder things than &quot;sleeps all day, never sees the sun&quot;.<br /> <br /> Add that albinism and porphyry are well known and documented since antiquity, again with a treatment to those in rich families very different to what's dispensed even today to some victims of &quot;ingredient harvesting&quot;.<br /> <br /> Until we got to the point of capturing on camera just how bad the weakness is, we'd have just too many other reasons to declare them preternatural inhuman monsters.<br /> <br /> VtR at least takes a detour by explaining first the particular apathy of the setting's mortals, and that communities that know vampires are a thing. There the Masquerade as a secret kept by a global conspiracy isn't a thing to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T01:39:19-07:00","id":1560749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560731#post1560731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know, but I don't think it big at all, not even 10th place.<br /> <br /> For the extent of their weakness to be even noticed you already have to go through a dozen or more other things that would have revealed them.<br /> <br /> People rarely or never seen during the day aren't that common. If you look the habits of rich and/or important people IRL through history you'll see several weirder things than &quot;sleeps all day, never sees the sun&quot;.<br /> <br /> Add that albinism and porphyry are well known and documented since antiquity, again with a treatment to those in rich families very different to what's dispensed even today to some victims of &quot;ingredient harvesting&quot;.<br /> <br /> Until we got to the point of capturing on camera just how bad the weakness is, we'd have just too many other reasons to declare them preternatural inhuman monsters.<br /> <br /> VtR at least takes a detour by explaining first the particular apathy of the setting's mortals, and that communities that know vampires are a thing. There the Masquerade as a secret kept by a global conspiracy isn't a thing to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. There's a lot of stuff that affects VtM that's just as big, if not bigger, a problem when placed in the context of a world that's historically being exceptionally hostile to all forms of special needs. Thus its not so much any one thing that'd cause the collapse of the house of cards, but rather several rocks forming an avalanche. All it waits for is that one incident to start it.<br /> <br /> As for albinos, they've been historically persecuted pretty badly due to their appearance. So that'd just leave a vtm vamp screwed even faster if they don't, or can't, mask their true nature. It should also be noted that modern scholars reject the idea of porphyry having anything to do with vampire beliefs due to lack of overlap between the folklore and the disease. So that idea appears to be entirely modern.<br /> <br /> And yeah aristocrats have always been weird as F. If anything they've gotten weirder and more brazen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T02:31:01-07:00","id":1560750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560749#post1560749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the context of a world that's historically being exceptionally hostile to all forms of special needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where I want to push back, not the core idea, but the lack of nuance. And importantly, ignoring that Vampire is already predicated on the idea that you can only count on yourself to cover your special needs, everyone else will just exploit them against you.<br /> <br /> I'm part of the disabled advocacy community and understand well what you mean. But the uniform approach loses a lot of details that not only historically matter, but here specifically matter to the stories we tell.<br /> <br /> First and most important, this has never been a uniform problem. Context matter, and power dynamics matter considerably. Ableism has so many times resulted in the children of the rich losing their privileges or lives for being disabled, but just as frequently or more they have gotten the adaptation denied to others.<br /> <br /> Especially if we're talking established adults. The same societies that abandoned mutilated people to poverty after a lifetime of services also left a rich record of prosthetic designs. The same societies that confined and isolated those who behaved weird, sometimes praised the same weirdness in someone else as a sign of genius or even divine favor.<br /> <br /> Add to it that the question isn't if vampires would be well adapted citizens. They're not even trying. It is if they would be noticed as vampires. They are getting their adaptations their way, not asking for them, and the premise is already secrecy about their condition, not acceptance.<br /> <br /> So the vampire would be found out for being pale and averse to sunlight? First, most would not be seen to begin with while they could avoid, people in general wouldn't know they're there. Then, an adult with aversion to sunlight is weird, but not unheard of, and would be pale as consequence. And sometimes work or other circumstance caused this.<br /> <br /> You'd need a lot of this vampire's preparations to fail to even get to the point where they're for real expected to get out during day, and then the vampire would first try to get away with any excuse not to, including pretending they already do, instead of saying it's a personal adaptation. Even today you can get away with that with &quot;made a religious oath&quot; or something, not to say how many adults can just say &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> Special needs only enter the picture after every barrier went down royally, and then who will deny the needs of someone who's already the richest in town and probably the boss of the boss of your boss? A vampire who really needs the society around them to respect the special needs on principle is already beyond screwed.<br /> <br /> The lack of accommodation for special needs is a terrible problem in our society. I'm currently myself fighting in the justice to get a few very basic accommodations I need for exceedingly well documented needs that have been neglected for years systematically in a company where they have negligible cost, just because the bureaucratic system is not built to make it happen.<br /> <br /> But the vampire as a hidden monster is not a creature that would particularly suffer this as a barrier to their conspiracy, when the conspiracy is already predicated on not revealing such needs. The accommodation can't be a cause of the revelation, because revelation has to occur first for accommodation to be required.<br /> <br /> Now, would it be a problem after the fact? For a vampire that's an overall common working class, definitely. For rich bastards that can buy their own accommodations, I don't think so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T12:42:03-07:00","id":1560768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560750#post1560750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's where I want to push back, not the core idea, but the lack of nuance. And importantly, ignoring that Vampire is already predicated on the idea that you can only count on yourself to cover your special needs, everyone else will just exploit them against you.<br /> <br /> I'm part of the disabled advocacy community and understand well what you mean. But the uniform approach loses a lot of details that not only historically matter, but here specifically matter to the stories we tell.<br /> <br /> First and most important, this has never been a uniform problem. Context matter, and power dynamics matter considerably. Ableism has so many times resulted in the children of the rich losing their privileges or lives for being disabled, but just as frequently or more they have gotten the adaptation denied to others.<br /> <br /> Especially if we're talking established adults. The same societies that abandoned mutilated people to poverty after a lifetime of services also left a rich record of prosthetic designs. The same societies that confined and isolated those who behaved weird, sometimes praised the same weirdness in someone else as a sign of genius or even divine favor.<br /> <br /> Add to it that the question isn't if vampires would be well adapted citizens. They're not even trying. It is if they would be noticed as vampires. They are getting their adaptations their way, not asking for them, and the premise is already secrecy about their condition, not acceptance.<br /> <br /> So the vampire would be found out for being pale and averse to sunlight? First, most would not be seen to begin with while they could avoid, people in general wouldn't know they're there. Then, an adult with aversion to sunlight is weird, but not unheard of, and would be pale as consequence. And sometimes work or other circumstance caused this.<br /> <br /> You'd need a lot of this vampire's preparations to fail to even get to the point where they're for real expected to get out during day, and then the vampire would first try to get away with any excuse not to, including pretending they already do, instead of saying it's a personal adaptation. Even today you can get away with that with &quot;made a religious oath&quot; or something, not to say how many adults can just say &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> Special needs only enter the picture after every barrier went down royally, and then who will deny the needs of someone who's already the richest in town and probably the boss of the boss of your boss? A vampire who really needs the society around them to respect the special needs on principle is already beyond screwed.<br /> <br /> The lack of accommodation for special needs is a terrible problem in our society. I'm currently myself fighting in the justice to get a few very basic accommodations I need for exceedingly well documented needs that have been neglected for years systematically in a company where they have negligible cost, just because the bureaucratic system is not built to make it happen.<br /> <br /> But the vampire as a hidden monster is not a creature that would particularly suffer this as a barrier to their conspiracy, when the conspiracy is already predicated on not revealing such needs. The accommodation can't be a cause of the revelation, because revelation has to occur first for accommodation to be required.<br /> <br /> Now, would it be a problem after the fact? For a vampire that's an overall common working class, definitely. For rich bastards that can buy their own accommodations, I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that those with immense privilege did sometimes manage to get things done to help. This is somewhat true for the non-rich too depending on the kind of family you were born into as well. If one wants to delve into the subject in depth, one will find a lot more nuance here and there. So I speak only in very general terms with the context of everything else vampires have to do in mind. For instance the amount of interaction they have with mortals is another thing to keep in mind. As is if they're trying to keep up some sort of mortal mask for one reason or another. Where they're doing this, etc etc. Easier to hide in a city crowd than the rural village where everyone knows everyone. Plus in the past it would've been much easier to get away with a lot of things since you didn't have spyware all over the place, nor nosy journalists or gossip mongers reporting on everything the wealthy do because that stuff sells. Honestly we could go on forever with what sort of challenges are present, how different factors impact them, what sort of efforts are needed to hide, etc etc etc. Because a single person has a much easier time to pull it off than a grand conspiracy like the masquerade as real life keep showing us.<br /> <br /> You have my empathy and sympathy. I live in Norway so I got lucky and didn't have to fight that much for mine. I wish that was true for others who are disabled or possess other special needs that need aid across the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T12:50:29-07:00","id":1560770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560721#post1560721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually kind of funny to think about how the length of time between the publication of Dracula and release of Nosferatu is short enough that Bram Stoker's widow was still alive (hence why she was able to get a court order for all copies of the film to be destroyed).<br /> <br /> Compared to the fact that the time between the release of the original Nosferatu movie and the most recent remake of it is longer than an entire century.<br /> <br /> Which is to say &quot;prior to the movie Nosferatu&quot; doesn't count for much when subsequent to the movie Nosferatu is longer than an entire century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonbg to lie, I love the idea one of the legal types helping Mrs Stoker with this case was Mr Jonathan Harker of DRACULA fame (with Mrs Harker and their surviving children on-hand to keep an eye out for Dangerous Occult Weirdness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T05:07:12-07:00","id":1560779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560768#post1560768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware that those with immense privilege did sometimes manage to get things done to help. This is somewhat true for the non-rich too depending on the kind of family you were born into as well. If one wants to delve into the subject in depth, one will find a lot more nuance here and there. So I speak only in very general terms with the context of everything else vampires have to do in mind. For instance the amount of interaction they have with mortals is another thing to keep in mind. As is if they're trying to keep up some sort of mortal mask for one reason or another. Where they're doing this, etc etc. Easier to hide in a city crowd than the rural village where everyone knows everyone. Plus in the past it would've been much easier to get away with a lot of things since you didn't have spyware all over the place, nor nosy journalists or gossip mongers reporting on everything the wealthy do because that stuff sells. Honestly we could go on forever with what sort of challenges are present, how different factors impact them, what sort of efforts are needed to hide, etc etc etc. Because a single person has a much easier time to pull it off than a grand conspiracy like the masquerade as real life keep showing us.<br /> <br /> You have my empathy and sympathy. I live in Norway so I got lucky and didn't have to fight that much for mine. I wish that was true for others who are disabled or possess other special needs that need aid across the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the game goes, the main point is that vampires already work with the idea that their special needs are a secret and a liability. So to me saying those needs would harm the Conspiracy isn't accurate because it's ignoring the basic premises of how this conspiracy work and what it does.<br /> <br /> A vampire that tries to pass as human or something isn't a demonstration of the problem, because the framework already assumes this character is a risk that needs special consideration.<br /> <br /> For my plight, don't worry. I live in Brazil, things are slow because bureaucracy, but we actually have worker laws, not like the cyberpunk dystopia up north between Mexico and Canada.<br /> <br /> I have plenty help in between like paid sick leaves however long I need, work stability, help from a Union as a legally mandated right rather than an org that has to survive busting attempts, free healthcare, free lawyer, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T05:16:22-07:00","id":1560780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560770#post1560770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not gonbg to lie, I love the idea one of the legal types helping Mrs Stoker with this case was Mr Jonathan Harker of DRACULA fame (with Mrs Harker and their surviving children on-hand to keep an eye out for Dangerous Occult Weirdness).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I imagine Mrs Stoker being helped by Barker with Dracula paying and going there as witness and co-victim.<br /> <br /> They won in the end 'cause Nosferatu refused to go in any session held during the day, while Harker could declare &quot;see, your honor? With all the emotional distress it causes him, my client still respects this court enough to hold his pain and come, trusting your judgment.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T03:53:50-07:00","id":1560810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560779#post1560779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the game goes, the main point is that vampires already work with the idea that their special needs are a secret and a liability. So to me saying those needs would harm the Conspiracy isn't accurate because it's ignoring the basic premises of how this conspiracy work and what it does.<br /> <br /> A vampire that tries to pass as human or something isn't a demonstration of the problem, because the framework already assumes this character is a risk that needs special consideration.<br /> <br /> For my plight, don't worry. I live in Brazil, things are slow because bureaucracy, but we actually have worker laws, not like the cyberpunk dystopia up north between Mexico and Canada.<br /> <br /> I have plenty help in between like paid sick leaves however long I need, work stability, help from a Union as a legally mandated right rather than an org that has to survive busting attempts, free healthcare, free lawyer, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I don't think we've really been disagreeing much outside of the finer details anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's good to hear. Here's hoping it gets even better in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T08:26:59-07:00","id":1560858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560197-why-is-the-vtm-version-of-the-sunlight-weakness-so-harsh?p=1560780#post1560780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, I imagine Mrs Stoker being helped by Barker with Dracula paying and going there as witness and co-victim.<br /> <br /> They won in the end 'cause Nosferatu refused to go in any session held during the day, while Harker could declare &quot;see, your honor? With all the emotional distress it causes him, my client still respects this court enough to hold his pain and come, trusting your judgment.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more in terms of the literary Harkers, who were \u2026 ummm \u2026 not very friendly to The Count (No matter what Hollywood tries to put across).<br /> <br /> Your take does sound very World of Darkness, though - hah! I\u2019ll bet this scenario keeps playing out in WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS territory too! (Bonus points if multiple vampires show up claiming to be THE Dracula).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}